# Run outputs live in runs/<id>/ and are deliberately NOT ignored — the whole
# point is that results accumulate and survive.
#
# These patterns are ANCHORED with a leading slash so they match only the stale
# top-level files left by the old script. Unanchored, `soak.log` would also match
# `runs/<id>/soak.log` and silently discard every run's evidence.
/soak.log
/chaos.log
/monitor.csv
/launch.log
/loadgen-stats.json
/runs/latest

# The repo root .gitignore has blanket `*.log` and `*.out` rules that otherwise
# swallow every run's soak.log, chaos.log, seizewatch.out and soakmon.log —
# exactly the evidence these directories exist to preserve. Re-include them.
# (Negation works because `runs/` itself is not ignored; git cannot re-include a
# file whose parent directory is excluded.)
!runs/**/*.log
!runs/**/*.out
!runs/**/*.csv
!runs/**/*.json
